To solve this, we first calculate the area of the rectangle defined by the vertices.
\begin{align*} \text{height} &= \textcolor{blue}{4} - \textcolor{red}{4} = 8 \\ \text{width} &= \textcolor{brown}{5} - \textcolor{purple}{-5} = 10 \end{align*}
Thus, the area of that region will be $8 \cdot 10$.
To have the points with integer coordinates that will be strictly in the interior of that rectangle,
\begin{align*} 8 \cdot 10 - 2\left(\textcolor{red}{5+1} + \textcolor{blue}{4+1} + \textcolor{brown}{5+1} + \textcolor{magenta}{4+1}\right) = 8 \cdot 10 - 2\left(6 + 5 + 6 + 5\right) \\ = 80 - 2\left(22\right) = 80 - 44 = 36.\end{align*}
So, there are $$36 \text{ points}$$ with integer coordinates that will be strictly in the interior of this rectangular region. </think> <answer>36</answer>

